## Operation: AddLocationFile

### Summary

A staff member uploads an image or a document to a location under one of its collection's media types.

### Input

```schema
locationId: string required ref(juicebar.locations#Location.id)
document: boolean required
mediaTypeKey: string required
file: file required
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.locations#Persona:LocationEditor`
- `juicebar.locations#Persona:LocationAdmin`
- `juicebar.locations#Persona:LocationSuperAdmin`

### Ensures

- The file is kept in the file store under the location, in `locations_documents` for a document and `locations` otherwise, and added to the location's files — [invokes](aim:juicebar#Capability:MediaStorage), [mutates](aim:juicebar.locations#Record:Location), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations.media#Requirements[LOCFILES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.core#Requirements[MEDIATYPES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.core#Requirements[MEDIASIZE])
- A notice tells whether it worked — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations.media#Requirements[FILESDONE])
- The operation is refused without the `updated` permission, or for a location of another organisation — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[LOCROLE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[ROLES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[LOCORG])

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/locations/details/location-media/location-media.component.ts#LocationMediaComponent.added` — as: component
- binds: `service:locations:service#addMedia` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred

## Operation: UpdateLocationFile

### Summary

A staff member changes a file's details: its name, title, description, alternative text and media type.

### Input

```schema
locationId: string required ref(juicebar.locations#Location.id)
mediaId: string required
key: string
mediaType: map(string)
name: map(string)
title: map(string)
description: map(string)
alt_text: map(string)
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.locations#Persona:LocationEditor`
- `juicebar.locations#Persona:LocationAdmin`
- `juicebar.locations#Persona:LocationSuperAdmin`

### Ensures

- The file's details are replaced with the ones given — [mutates](aim:juicebar.locations#Record:Location), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.core#Requirements[MEDIALIST])
- A notice tells whether it worked — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations.media#Requirements[FILESDONE])
- The operation is refused without the `updated` permission, or for a location of another organisation — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[LOCROLE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[ROLES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[LOCORG])

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/locations/details/location-media/location-media.component.ts#LocationMediaComponent.updated` — as: component
- binds: `service:locations:service#updateMedia` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred

## Operation: RemoveLocationFile

### Summary

A staff member removes a file from a location.

### Input

```schema
locationId: string required ref(juicebar.locations#Location.id)
mediaId: string required
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.locations#Persona:LocationEditor`
- `juicebar.locations#Persona:LocationAdmin`
- `juicebar.locations#Persona:LocationSuperAdmin`

### Expects

- The staff member confirmed the removal.

### Ensures

- The file is no longer among the location's files — [mutates](aim:juicebar.locations#Record:Location), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.core#Requirements[MEDIALIST]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations.media#Requirements[FILESDONE])
- The operation is refused without the `updated` permission, or for a location of another organisation — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[LOCROLE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[ROLES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[LOCORG])

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/locations/details/location-media/location-media.component.ts#LocationMediaComponent.removed` — as: component
- binds: `service:locations:service#removeMedia` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred
